derivations.claim:
Let $(E_r(x))_{r>0}$ be a family of Borel sets shrinking nicely to $x$ with constant $\alpha_x>0$. Then $$ rac{
u(E_r(x))}{\lambda(E_r(x))}= rac{1}{\lambda(E_r(x))}\int_{E_r(x)}f\,d\lambda+ rac{
u_s(E_r(x))}{\lambda(E_r(x))},$$ while positivity and the defining comparison give $$0\le rac{
u_s(E_r(x))}{\lambda(E_r(x))}\le rac{1}{\alpha_x} rac{
u_s(B(x,r))}{\lambda(B(x,r))}.$$ Consequently [L2] and step 1.1 reduce both conclusions to proving $$ rac{
u_s(B(x,r))}{\lambda(B(x,r))}\longrightarrow0$$ for almost every $x$.
